{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/877776-interest-check-recruitment-tremere-conversion-playtest-vtr-2e","id":877776,"title":"[Interest Check/Recruitment] Tremere Conversion Playtest [VtR 2e]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play","Play by Post"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-29T09:14:40-07:00","id":877776,"title":"[Interest Check/Recruitment] Tremere Conversion Playtest [VtR 2e]","content":"So, with Mage 2e coming out soon, obviously that means now's the time to seek out interest in a Vampire the Requiem game! More seriously, I wanted to see if I could put together an interesting game using my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-vI88bjgHoXUa5_0qLKQIdMMMKknoUhvFCLzSY7nrOE/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Tremere &quot;bloodline&quot;</a> and playtest them for mechanical concerns in the process. Lacking the actual Mage 2e pdf yet, obviously there's still a few missing mechanics in there, but I intend to fill them out straightaway. This thread, for now, is just to see if I have anyone interested in such a game before I go spending too much effort fleshing such a thing out.<br /> <br /> My basic idea is to set it in a small city, like Portland, Maine, a place that likely has a minimal Vampiric presence but by contrast, has a comparatively large number of Mages, due to an unusual number of supernatural happenstances there; there's no single Mystery, just a lot of 'weird crap' that goes on. The job of the group, then, will be to help catalog some of it and to see what can be drawn into the local House's auspice (for the sake of the Council's goals, of course). Knowing me, you can expect some crossover regarding said Mysteries. I'll obviously add more details, again, once I have Mage 2e and once I'm sure I have interest.<br /> <br /> Ruleswise, I'll probably give you guys a handful of starting Experiences, and maybe a free dot or two of Paths. I'd also allow you to use other stuff on my homebrew that'd mesh; <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1gfFNSeOv-xvhM1cC6h9Zfpyt11XcmIUvtCjbgSmYWgg/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Sanguine Craft</a>, for instance, but obviously no bloodlines since you'll already be part of one inherently. (Once more, actual specifics can wait until I have interest)<br /> <br /> I don't think I have the focus for a huge game, so I'm thinking 3 players to start with, on a 'first interesting concept, first serve' basis. That is, saying &quot;I want in&quot; doesn't reserve a spot (though is still helpful in proving there's interest to me), but posting an obviously thought out concept does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":1130,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","user":"falco1029","date":". 04-29-2016, 12:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T10:56:14-07:00","id":883901,"title":"","content":"Just going to mention that with Mage out, the document's been updated 